Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.98,0:00:21.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[guests chattering]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.37,0:00:33.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is that her?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.33,0:00:36.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The incomparable{\i0}\N{\i1}who captured the prince's eye.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.67,0:00:39.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A mere wisp of a young lady,{\i0}\N{\i1}and a commoner at that.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.01,0:00:45.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Everyone seems to have quite an opinion.{\i0}\N{\i1}[chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.97,0:00:49.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}How long do you think it will be{\i0}\N{\i1}before Her Majesty arrives?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.35,0:00:51.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I may very well faint from hunger.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.39,0:00:56.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mama! We are at court!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.90,0:00:58.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}No one is looking at me, dearest.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.36,0:01:00.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mama!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.36,0:01:02.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That's quite delicious. [laughs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.07,0:01:05.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My darling, you seem a little strained.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.86,0:01:07.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You have been that way{\i0}\N{\i1}for the past few days.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.78,0:01:09.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I have much on my mind.{\i0}\N{\i1}-You do, indeed.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.82,0:01:10.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[doors open]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.45,0:01:13.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Her Majesty Queen Charlotte{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.16,0:01:16.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and her esteemed nephew,{\i0}\N{\i1}Prince Friedrich of Prussia.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.33,0:01:17.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[regal music plays]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.80,0:01:28.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Miss Bridgerton, I find myself in raptures{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.89,0:01:31.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}over your acceptance{\i0}\N{\i1}of my invitation to the palace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.76,0:01:33.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You flatter me, Your Highness.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.68,0:01:36.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I cannot help it.{\i0}\N{\i1}You are perfection itself.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.31,0:01:37.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Offer her your gift.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.69,0:01:40.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have brought you a gift.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.11,0:01:43.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[exclaims softly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.40,0:01:45.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[guests gasp, murmur]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.28,0:01:54.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[mournful piano music plays]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.33,0:02:02.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne sighs, echoing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.72,0:02:10.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne gasps]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.05,0:02:12.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Miss Bridgerton, are you unwell?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.97,0:02:17.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am perfectly well. Of course.{\i0}\N{\i1}[breathes tremulously]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.27,0:02:18.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This necklace is…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.64,0:02:20.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}quite well too.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.98,0:02:23.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She will make a lovely princess,{\i0}\N{\i1}will she not?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.15,0:02:24.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of course, Your Majesty.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.15,0:02:27.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[chuckles softly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.41,0:02:38.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Whistledown]{\i0}\N<span style="style2">{\an8}In a town filled with ambitious mamas{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.25,0:02:40.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8}{\i1}and fortune-hunting gentlemen,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.87,0:02:43.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}marrying above one's station{\i0}\N{\i1}is an art form, indeed.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.67,0:02:47.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But Miss Daphne Bridgerton's advance{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.67,0:02:50.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}from future duchess to possible princess{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.63,0:02:54.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}is an achievement{\i0}\N{\i1}that even this jaded author must applaud.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.64,0:02:58.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is it true?{\i0}\N{\i1}Am I to be the sister of a princess?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.52,0:02:59.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Calm yourself.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.64,0:03:01.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am not yet engaged to the prince.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.64,0:03:03.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Will you have to wear a crown?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.31,0:03:06.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps for special occasions,{\i0}\N{\i1}but only if I should marry the prince.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.86,0:03:08.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Will you have to learn Prussian?{\i0}\N{\i1}-It is German.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.78,0:03:11.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And perhaps,{\i0}\N{\i1}but only if I should marry the prince.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.53,0:03:14.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Will you have to move{\i0}\N{\i1}to a castle far, far away?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.49,0:03:16.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Should you not be off somewhere{\i0}\N{\i1}with your governess?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.66,0:03:20.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I should. My governess has{\i0}\N{\i1}the very same questions as me!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.62,0:03:22.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sighs sharply]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.58,0:03:25.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Whistledown]{\i0}\N<span style="style2">Though this author cannot dismiss{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.29,0:03:27.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the Duke of Hastings quite so soon.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.13,0:03:31.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He may have let the diamond{\i0}\N{\i1}slip through his fingers for now,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.05,0:03:36.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but I shall wager he is not a man{\i0}\N{\i1}to ever hide from a fight.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.31,0:03:41.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon grunting rapidly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.56,0:03:48.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Does that sack of grain{\i0}\N{\i1}have a German accent,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.48,0:03:50.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}or is it my imagination?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.19,0:03:51.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Remind me, Will…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.95,0:03:54.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}are you participating{\i0}\N{\i1}in a boxing exhibition today,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.78,0:03:56.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}or is it a comedy exhibition?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.45,0:03:58.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I was afraid you had forgotten.{\i0}\N{\i1}-I had not.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.53,0:04:01.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Although I am afraid{\i0}\N{\i1}you will have to soldier on{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.58,0:04:03.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}without your greatest admirer present{\i0}\N{\i1}this afternoon.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.71,0:04:05.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Alice will be present.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.21,0:04:07.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am leaving England. [panting]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.38,0:04:09.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My business is concluded.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.71,0:04:12.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Will's is not.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.09,0:04:13.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This will be{\i0}\N{\i1}the biggest match of my career.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.84,0:04:15.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I am not favored to win it.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Will--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.47,0:04:17.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your smart friends know{\i0}\N{\i1}you frequent my saloon.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.55,0:04:19.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Who will wager on me{\i0}\N{\i1}if you are not present?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.22,0:04:21.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I don't have any friends.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.93,0:04:23.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}How about after the Irishman today, Will,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.69,0:04:26.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}you pummel the piss{\i0}\N{\i1}out of His Grace's self-pity?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.90,0:04:29.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have never asked a favor,{\i0}\N{\i1}but I implore you not to miss this match.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.73,0:04:31.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}His Grace would like to miss{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.36,0:04:34.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the chance of seeing the Bridgerton girl{\i0}\N{\i1}on the arm of a prince.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.28,0:04:35.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps you're right.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.53,0:04:37.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Both of you understand{\i0}\N{\i1}I am just here, do you?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.87,0:04:39.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am not nearly as devoted{\i0}\N{\i1}as the two of you,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.74,0:04:41.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}along with Lady Whistledown,{\i0}\N{\i1}would like to believe.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.87,0:04:44.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The only thing we are devoted to{\i0}\N{\i1}is putting food in our children's mouths.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.04,0:04:47.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps you'd like to dig{\i0}\N{\i1}a little deeper today, Your Grace,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.67,0:04:49.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and help us fatten{\i0}\N{\i1}the match organizer's purses{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.88,0:04:50.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}as well as ours?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.26,0:04:53.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.88,0:04:55.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You don't love me for my subtlety.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.72,0:05:00.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon sighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.76,0:05:01.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[horse neighing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.19,0:05:13.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[grunts]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.90,0:05:15.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Her needlework is divine.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.61,0:05:19.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And, of course, she sings{\i0}\N{\i1}and plays the pianoforte very prettily.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.62,0:05:20.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Show me a smile, girl.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.53,0:05:22.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I beg your pardon?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.66,0:05:24.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your teeth, I want to see them.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.12,0:05:26.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is she simpleminded?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.25,0:05:28.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Goodness, no! Oh, you are droll!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.58,0:05:32.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Miss Thompson, um,{\i0}\N{\i1}show Lord Rutledge your lovely smile.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.92,0:05:35.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Miss Thompson?{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Rutledge grunts]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.84,0:05:38.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Tell a lot from a person's mouth.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.35,0:05:41.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Soldiers' teeth.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.80,0:05:43.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Taken from the battlefield.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.26,0:05:45.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Cost a pretty penny, let me tell you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.23,0:05:50.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I shall try her out in company,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.23,0:05:53.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}see how she acquits herself.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.98,0:05:54.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of course.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.98,0:05:57.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We will be attending the Trowbridge ball{\i0}\N{\i1}this evening, naturally.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.82,0:05:59.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, very well.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.07,0:06:01.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Good day, Featherington.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.20,0:06:03.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Rutledge.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.87,0:06:05.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You cannot be serious.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.41,0:06:07.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}How dare you conduct yourself{\i0}\N{\i1}in such brazen manner?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.00,0:06:11.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Do you see now what I must endure daily?{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Lord Featherington] Mm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.17,0:06:13.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have had suitors calling on me{\i0}\N{\i1}every morning this week.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.88,0:06:15.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you think{\i0}\N{\i1}I'm going to marry that vile old--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.88,0:06:19.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Those suitors are courting you, my dear.{\i0}\N{\i1}That could take weeks, months.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.22,0:06:22.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Even if a miracle occurred,{\i0}\N{\i1}and one of them married you tomorrow,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.80,0:06:24.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}how do you imagine{\i0}\N{\i1}they would react six months hence{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.89,0:06:28.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}when that whelp of yours pops out{\i0}\N{\i1}looking the picture of health?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.39,0:06:30.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Lord Rutledge is in want of an heir.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.94,0:06:32.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He will not ask questions.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.77,0:06:34.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Marina huffs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.44,0:06:38.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[scoffs] She pushed me!{\i0}\N{\i1}-No, she pushed me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.03,0:06:41.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Hush, both of you! My nerves!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.25,0:06:48.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Marina?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.12,0:06:51.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Would you like me to stay in?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.71,0:06:57.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Kindly remind me, my lord,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.05,0:07:01.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}why we cannot simply send Miss Thompson{\i0}\N{\i1}back to her father in the country?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.63,0:07:03.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The matter is not for discussion.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.22,0:07:05.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A gentleman caller. Mr. Albion Finch.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.35,0:07:12.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Good day. [sneezes]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.90,0:07:17.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[gasps] Daisies always trouble my nose.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.90,0:07:20.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Miss Thompson is not receiving visitors,{\i0}\N{\i1}Mr. Finch.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.11,0:07:21.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That is quite all right.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.70,0:07:23.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am here to call on Miss Featherington.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.91,0:07:28.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Miss Philippa Featherington?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.95,0:07:30.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[exhales nervously]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.47,0:07:42.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Thank you, sir.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.68,0:07:44.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.80,0:07:46.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[exhales contentedly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.14,0:07:50.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have never understood{\i0}\N{\i1}the fashion for feathers in the hair.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.98,0:07:53.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why would a woman want to draw notice{\i0}\N{\i1}to the fact that she is like a bird{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.98,0:07:56.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}squawking for a man's attention{\i0}\N{\i1}in some bizarre ritual?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.77,0:07:58.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Then why are we looking?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.19,0:08:01.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Because I would rather do anything{\i0}\N{\i1}than stay a moment longer in that house{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.15,0:08:03.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}while everyone flutters around Daphne,{\i0}\N{\i1}cooing over her prospects.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.07,0:08:06.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is the prince still courting? I imagine{\i0}\N{\i1}you cannot wait for the engagement.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.07,0:08:09.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Pen, once they are engaged,{\i0}\N{\i1}I shall be next in line.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.66,0:08:11.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If anything,{\i0}\N{\i1}I hope Daphne stays on the shelf forever.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.91,0:08:13.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She must marry eventually.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.50,0:08:15.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why must our only options be{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.50,0:08:17.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to squawk and settle{\i0}\N{\i1}or to never leave the nest?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.88,0:08:20.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What if I want to fly?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.96,0:08:22.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[scoffs] You know who {\i0}<span style="style2">is{\i0}{\i1} flying?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.88,0:08:25.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Lady Whistledown. She is up in the sky.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.43,0:08:28.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A brilliant woman of business{\i0}\N{\i1}who fools the entire ton,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.22,0:08:29.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}whilst pocketing their money.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.93,0:08:31.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Imagine the life she must lead.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.60,0:08:32.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Independence.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.52,0:08:36.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She is not simpering{\i0}\N{\i1}on the edge of a ballroom every night,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.35,0:08:39.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}praying a man might take a fancy{\i0}\N{\i1}and leg-shackle her into marriage.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.19,0:08:41.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That is quite the life{\i0}\N{\i1}you have imagined for her.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.53,0:08:44.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We must meet her{\i0}\N{\i1}so that she might share her secrets{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.82,0:08:47.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}on how to avoid such a wretched,{\i0}\N{\i1}uninteresting fate.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.37,0:08:49.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Lady Whistledown's identity{\i0}\N{\i1}is quite protected.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.58,0:08:51.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Are we not the two most clever girls{\i0}\N{\i1}in the ton?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.58,0:08:53.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If anyone can find her, it is us, I think.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.62,0:08:56.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If I could get out of any{\i0}\N{\i1}of the week's events to help you, I would.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.92,0:08:59.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Pretend an illness.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.21,0:09:01.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Tell your mother{\i0}\N{\i1}you caught whatever Marina had.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.67,0:09:04.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-How is she, by the way?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Uh, recovering.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.05,0:09:06.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But it would be cruel of me{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.76,0:09:09.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}not to be by her side{\i0}\N{\i1}when she comes back out.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.18,0:09:11.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I shall cheer you on{\i0}\N{\i1}in your endeavors, though.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.43,0:09:13.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This one. I shall need a new quill{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.22,0:09:14.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to make my list of suspects.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.73,0:09:16.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Ooh! Thank you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.60,0:09:18.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[attendees clamoring]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.73,0:09:20.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[bookkeeper] Come on, then!{\i0}\N{\i1}Is it Mondrich or Gillespie?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.94,0:09:22.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Thank you, sir!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.90,0:09:27.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne] If Mama knew{\i0}\N{\i1}I were here, of all places…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.70,0:09:30.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Anthony] Trust she would have{\i0}\N{\i1}more to say to me than you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.24,0:09:36.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There's your prince now.{\i0}\N{\i1}With your fancy well in hand,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.12,0:09:38.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I shall make myself scarce{\i0}\N{\i1}for the final blow.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.92,0:09:45.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Miss Bridgerton, I am delighted{\i0}\N{\i1}to see you here today, though surprised.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.34,0:09:48.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Though I asked your brother to bring you{\i0}\N{\i1}so we could spend some time together,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.59,0:09:50.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I admit I did not hold much hope.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.18,0:09:53.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Most ladies I have met cannot seem{\i0}\N{\i1}to reconcile their delicate sensibilities{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.06,0:09:55.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}with the brutality of fights.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.31,0:09:57.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You must have no sisters, Your Highness,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.89,0:10:00.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}if you think most women delicate and mild.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.69,0:10:03.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A trip to the modiste{\i0}\N{\i1}during a silk shortage{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.19,0:10:05.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}would disabuse you{\i0}\N{\i1}of such notions for good.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.44,0:10:06.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both chuckle]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.74,0:10:08.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I suppose I have much to learn, then.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.99,0:10:11.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I would appreciate your expert tutelage{\i0}\N{\i1}if you would join me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.37,0:10:15.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[mournful music plays]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.04,0:10:17.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Miss Bridgerton?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.16,0:10:20.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of course. I would be delighted.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.54,0:10:26.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Tell us, Mr. Mondrich, is it true{\i0}\N{\i1}you've been training with the duke?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.59,0:10:29.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Let us not exaggerate my role.{\i0}\N{\i1}I am a mere pupil.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.26,0:10:31.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Target practice, at best.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Will] His Grace is modest.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.51,0:10:34.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He's one of the least pitiful students{\i0}\N{\i1}I have ever trained.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.35,0:10:35.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[men laughing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.02,0:10:38.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Will] You'd do well following his lead{\i0}\N{\i1}and wagering on me today.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.85,0:10:40.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is that not right, Hastings?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.31,0:10:44.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Hastings?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Of course.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.48,0:10:47.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Our underdog, Mr. Mondrich,{\i0}\N{\i1}shall emerge victorious.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.53,0:10:49.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I, for one,{\i0}\N{\i1}have 40 shillings on Mr. Gillespie.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.99,0:10:52.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}After all, he is the prince's man.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.16,0:10:55.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[announcer] Ladies and gentlemen,{\i0}\N{\i1}please take your seats!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.58,0:10:57.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-The match is to begin!{\i0}\N{\i1}-[bell rings]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.16,0:10:59.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[crowd cheering, jeering]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.87,0:11:00.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon] Watch him!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.13,0:11:05.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[crowd exclaims]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.67,0:11:08.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fear not. My man is made of sterner stuff.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.42,0:11:10.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Will groans]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.47,0:11:13.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Yes, again!{\i0}\N{\i1}-Come on, Mondrich! Watch your feet!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.27,0:11:20.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[playful music plays]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.10,0:11:25.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[music, no dialogue]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.69,0:11:31.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[music ends]{\i0}\N{\i1}-[crowd jeering loudly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.49,0:11:39.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You must tell me, Your Highness,{\i0}\N{\i1}do you miss your homeland?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.91,0:11:43.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have never been to Prussia,{\i0}\N{\i1}but I have read of its beauty.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.42,0:11:45.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It has attractions, to be sure.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.21,0:11:47.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That said,{\i0}\N{\i1}I attended school here in England,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.67,0:11:50.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and I have often thought{\i0}\N{\i1}there is no better place to live,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.72,0:11:51.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}or to raise a family.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.01,0:11:56.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Uh, forgive me if I am too forthright,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.43,0:11:58.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but you have a great affinity{\i0}\N{\i1}for your family, do you not?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.89,0:12:02.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I do. They are{\i0}\N{\i1}the dearest thing in the world to me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.77,0:12:03.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Are you close to yours?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.89,0:12:05.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I grew up{\i0}\N{\i1}with many cousins running underfoot{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.98,0:12:09.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and I believe I should like the same{\i0}\N{\i1}for my children one day…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.61,0:12:12.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}if my wife were amenable, of course.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.17,0:12:27.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[crowd cheers]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.00,0:12:30.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Come on, Billy!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.13,0:12:31.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Go on, Mondrich!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.17,0:12:33.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Focus, Mondrich! Get your wits about you!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.38,0:12:38.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Go on, Gillespie! Plant a facer!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.77,0:12:41.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Good man! Another!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.43,0:12:43.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[grunting]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.89,0:12:44.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[crowd cheers]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.56,0:12:46.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne exclaims]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.49,0:12:57.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[bell rings]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.82,0:12:59.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[crowd cheers loudly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.45,0:13:01.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Anthony] Go on, Mondrich!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.75,0:13:10.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[inaudible dialogue]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.26,0:13:18.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[man] You guaranteed my money.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Gentlemen!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.34,0:13:21.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I assure you, on my good name,{\i0}\N{\i1}each of you will receive your payments.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.06,0:13:24.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I merely need two days to raise the blunt.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.56,0:13:27.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[men murmuring]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.40,0:13:31.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Henry] What do you think, Bridgerton?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.40,0:13:33.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This one more to your liking?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.36,0:13:34.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mr. Granville--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.49,0:13:36.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps they should take it{\i0}\N{\i1}over to Somerset House{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.70,0:13:39.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}so it can be skyed right next to mine.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.32,0:13:41.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I believe I owe you an apology, sir.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.33,0:13:43.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Unnecessary.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.87,0:13:46.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I actually quite enjoy{\i0}\N{\i1}the eloquent stings of your critique.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.33,0:13:47.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Benedict] Mm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.79,0:13:48.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}So?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.46,0:13:51.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A touch morose for my tastes.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.54,0:13:52.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Henry] Mm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.09,0:13:54.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Henry inhales]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.01,0:13:57.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A tragedy. The hound deserved better.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.34,0:13:59.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[laughs] Where is yours?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.14,0:14:01.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-My…{\i0}\N{\i1}-Your work.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.31,0:14:05.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Are you to tell me{\i0}\N{\i1}you're not an artist yourself?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.35,0:14:07.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, I-- I suppose sometimes I like to…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.81,0:14:09.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, I mean, I almost--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.48,0:14:12.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I believe "yes" and "thank you"{\i0}\N{\i1}are the words you seek.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.73,0:14:16.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But either way,{\i0}\N{\i1}you should come by my studio.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.28,0:14:20.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The pieces I do for myself are there,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.57,0:14:23.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and I think you will find{\i0}\N{\i1}my real work far less, um…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.16,0:14:27.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, how did you put it?{\i0}\N{\i1}"Cold and lacking inner life"?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.66,0:14:30.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mm. I shall never live that down, shall I?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.50,0:14:32.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[chuckles]{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Henry] Hmm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.21,0:14:33.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Benedict laughs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.55,0:14:43.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I hear you are to leave town tonight.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.39,0:14:45.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You hear correctly.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.85,0:14:49.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I misjudged you.{\i0}\N{\i1}I was never quite certain,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.44,0:14:52.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but now it is clear your intentions{\i0}\N{\i1}with Daphne were honorable after all.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.40,0:14:55.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She has found herself a prince,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.82,0:14:57.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and you are going on your way.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.49,0:15:01.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps one day the two of us{\i0}\N{\i1}will be able to laugh at all this?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.86,0:15:02.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.99,0:15:05.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Are you to tell me{\i0}\N{\i1}you're sorry to see me go?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.04,0:15:08.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We should not have{\i0}\N{\i1}to go that far, should we?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.45,0:15:09.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.21,0:15:15.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Lord Bridgerton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.84,0:15:16.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your Highness.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.50,0:15:19.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I was told you would be here.{\i0}\N{\i1}Might we have a word?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.84,0:15:20.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Benedict] Certainly.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.93,0:15:26.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[inaudible dialogue]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.39,0:15:33.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your brother took you where?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.06,0:15:36.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He kept close watch{\i0}\N{\i1}the entire time, Mama.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.69,0:15:40.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It does not matter. A boxing exhibition{\i0}\N{\i1}is no place for any young lady.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.86,0:15:43.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is it a place for a prince?{\i0}\N{\i1}Was he at today's match, Sister?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.07,0:15:44.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He certainly was.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.99,0:15:47.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is a loathsome{\i0}\N{\i1}and barbarous form of entertainment.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.33,0:15:49.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-What about the duke?{\i0}\N{\i1}-[both] What about the duke?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.33,0:15:53.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Was he also present?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.08,0:15:55.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I do not know.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.58,0:15:57.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If the duke was there, I did not see him.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.84,0:15:59.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[playing classical piano tune]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.09,0:16:05.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-What are you writing?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Nothing. [clears throat]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.14,0:16:07.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You sit about,{\i0}\N{\i1}writing nothing all day long.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.47,0:16:09.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sighs] I am telling Francesca{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.10,0:16:10.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}about what an officious{\i0}\N{\i1}little busybody you are.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.06,0:16:12.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[chuckles ironically]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.36,0:16:17.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mother. Daph.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.02,0:16:20.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Did you truly take your sister{\i0}\N{\i1}to a boxing match?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.11,0:16:22.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your admonishment will have to wait.{\i0}\N{\i1}I have news.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.15,0:16:25.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Prince Friedrich has asked{\i0}\N{\i1}for my permission to propose.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.62,0:16:27.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}So soon?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.12,0:16:29.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, what did you tell him?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.83,0:16:32.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That I know better{\i0}\N{\i1}than to answer for my sister.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.12,0:16:34.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have no objections to the man.{\i0}\N{\i1}People speak well of him.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.79,0:16:38.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Whatever you decide, Daph,{\i0}\N{\i1}you shall have my support.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.38,0:16:40.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[tense music plays]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.26,0:16:45.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I… uh…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.88,0:16:47.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I… [sighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.80,0:16:49.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You need not decide now.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.35,0:16:51.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You have not known him long.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.02,0:16:54.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Let me know when you have an answer,{\i0}\N{\i1}and I shall convey it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.10,0:16:55.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Indeed.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.66,0:17:14.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is quite a necklace. [chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.83,0:17:18.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do you like it?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.71,0:17:21.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is very beautiful.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.25,0:17:22.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But do you like it?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.76,0:17:27.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you should have something to say,{\i0}\N{\i1}Mama, please say it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.38,0:17:28.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, I only wonder…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.18,0:17:34.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you wear that necklace at{\i0}\N{\i1}tonight's ball, what will the duke think?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.93,0:17:35.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, Mama!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.85,0:17:38.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Until you have decided{\i0}\N{\i1}to accept the prince's proposal,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.15,0:17:40.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I simply think{\i0}\N{\i1}you should keep your mind open.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.31,0:17:43.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mama, I do not care what the duke thinks.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.82,0:17:46.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Besides,{\i0}\N{\i1}he will not even be at tonight's ball.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.99,0:17:49.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-What happened between the two of you?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Nothing happened.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.74,0:17:51.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He is leaving.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.66,0:17:54.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know my daughter.{\i0}\N{\i1}I know it was not nothing between you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.54,0:17:55.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You do not know.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.16,0:17:57.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You do not know anything.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.54,0:17:59.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Daphne, I know what I saw!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.21,0:18:00.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What you saw…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.34,0:18:02.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}was a lie.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.46,0:18:06.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.59,0:18:08.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It was a lie.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.22,0:18:11.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It was a ruse.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.93,0:18:16.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The… duke and I, we were pretending,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.18,0:18:19.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}all so I could attract{\i0}\N{\i1}a suitor of a high enough rank,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.02,0:18:22.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}all so I could be that much more…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.69,0:18:23.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}desirable.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.94,0:18:27.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It was an agreement.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.19,0:18:29.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It was an act, and it worked.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.66,0:18:30.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We got what we wanted.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.03,0:18:32.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You did, too. I now have a prince.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.62,0:18:34.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You should be proud.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.70,0:18:38.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What I wanted, dearest,{\i0}\N{\i1}was for you to have the best,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.16,0:18:40.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}not in terms of rank, but love.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.50,0:18:42.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And what I have seen{\i0}\N{\i1}between you and the duke--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.84,0:18:44.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It was not real, Mama!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.76,0:18:48.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Everything you saw…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.80,0:18:50.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}None of it was real.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.30,0:18:54.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, it…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.51,0:18:55.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is over now.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.77,0:19:00.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[voice breaking]{\i0}\N{\i1}I do not have to pretend any longer.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.36,0:19:10.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am sorry, Mama.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.70,0:19:13.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am so sorry. [sobs lightly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.95,0:19:20.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is a beautiful necklace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.37,0:19:24.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I should like it very much.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.22,0:19:36.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Danbury]{\i0}\N{\i1}I would tell you it's been lovely{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.26,0:19:38.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}spending all this time{\i0}\N{\i1}with you, Your Grace,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.14,0:19:40.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but I tend to leave{\i0}\N{\i1}such sycophantic behavior{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.02,0:19:42.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}for the rest of the ton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.52,0:19:44.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I shall miss you, too, Lady Danbury.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.15,0:19:48.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Are you going to tell me{\i0}\N{\i1}where you will go?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.69,0:19:49.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This time, that is.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.90,0:19:51.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am still considering, but--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.57,0:19:53.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It does not really matter, does it?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.32,0:19:56.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am sure you will abscond{\i0}\N{\i1}to some remote corner of the world{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.16,0:19:58.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and continue to do{\i0}\N{\i1}what you have always done.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.58,0:20:02.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-And what would that be?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Take everything you have for granted.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.00,0:20:07.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The young man{\i0}\N{\i1}I have always taken pride in raising,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.38,0:20:08.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}well…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.63,0:20:11.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I would have expected more.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.38,0:20:15.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}More discernment,{\i0}\N{\i1}more understanding, more appreciation.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.93,0:20:16.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Lady Danbury--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.85,0:20:20.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You allowed that young lady{\i0}\N{\i1}to slip through your fingers{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.18,0:20:21.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}as if it were nothing.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.27,0:20:25.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I understand that you believe{\i0}\N{\i1}such subjects as love and devotion,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.94,0:20:27.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}affection and attachment,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.52,0:20:29.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}you find it all trite and frivolous.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.94,0:20:34.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But have you any idea those very things{\i0}\N{\i1}are precisely what have allowed{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.20,0:20:37.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}a new day to begin to dawn{\i0}\N{\i1}in this society?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.49,0:20:40.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Look at our queen.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.58,0:20:43.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Look at our king. Look at their marriage.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.00,0:20:47.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Look at everything it is doing for us,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.63,0:20:49.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}allowing us to become.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.34,0:20:53.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We were two separate societies,{\i0}\N{\i1}divided by color,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.01,0:20:57.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}until a king fell in love with one of us.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.14,0:21:00.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Love, Your Grace…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.56,0:21:03.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}conquers all.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.48,0:21:07.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I believe that remains to be seen.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.06,0:21:11.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The king may have chosen his queen.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.86,0:21:13.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He may have elevated us{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.11,0:21:15.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}from novelties in their eyes{\i0}\N{\i1}to now dukes and royalty,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.90,0:21:17.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and at that same whim…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.45,0:21:20.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}he may just as easily change his mind,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.74,0:21:25.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}a mind, as we all know, that is hanging on{\i0}\N{\i1}by one very loose and tenuous thread.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.12,0:21:28.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}So, no, I am sorry, Lady Danbury,{\i0}\N{\i1}we are in disagreement here.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.17,0:21:30.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Love changes nothing.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.51,0:21:37.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My ship departs at quarter past nine.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.22,0:21:40.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I will write to you…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.76,0:21:42.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}from wherever I go.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.02,0:21:50.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}["Second Waltz"{\i0}\N{\i1}by Dmitri Shostakovich plays]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.06,0:21:52.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Whistledown] {\i0}<span style="style2">As we all know,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:52.86,0:21:56.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}there is nothing this author loves{\i0}\N{\i1}more than a scandal,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.86,0:22:00.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and tonight's soiree promises{\i0}\N{\i1}more than its fair share,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:00.74,0:22:04.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}courtesy of the recently widowed{\i0}\N{\i1}Lady Trowbridge.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:04.41,0:22:07.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Some may call{\i0}\N{\i1}her celebrations too provocative,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.50,0:22:09.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and I would caution any young lady{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:09.29,0:22:13.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}from getting caught up{\i0}\N{\i1}in the sensual nature of her fêtes.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:13.30,0:22:16.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}For one scandalous move{\i0}\N{\i1}between an unwed couple,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:16.72,0:22:20.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}a wayward touch, or heaven forbid, a kiss,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:20.14,0:22:24.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}would banish any young lady{\i0}\N{\i1}from society in a trail of ruin.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:27.43,0:22:28.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Lord Rutledge.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:30.52,0:22:34.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Miss Thompson{\i0}\N{\i1}has spent all afternoon telling us{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:34.11,0:22:36.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}how eager she is to converse with you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:36.90,0:22:41.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I don't need her conversation.{\i0}\N{\i1}I shall like to see how she spins.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:43.95,0:22:45.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sneezes]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:46.54,0:22:48.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Mr. Finch.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Pardon me, Miss Featherington.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:49.04,0:22:51.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[chuckles]{\i0}\N{\i1}-Oh! What a delectable frock!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:51.46,0:22:53.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Almost the exact shade{\i0}\N{\i1}of double Gloucester{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:53.54,0:22:55.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}your mother served at tea this afternoon.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:55.21,0:22:57.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I so love cheese.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:58.13,0:23:00.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-As do I, Mr. Finch. [chuckles]{\i0}\N{\i1}-[laughs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:00.55,0:23:03.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Though, I must say,{\i0}\N{\i1}I do prefer a Stilton to a cheddar.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.68,0:23:07.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[Albion chuckles]{\i0}\N{\i1}-Mm!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:09.68,0:23:12.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps we will have two weddings{\i0}\N{\i1}this season, my lord.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:12.65,0:23:13.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, I do doubt that.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.91,0:23:28.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Daphne! [chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:29.54,0:23:32.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-You look beautiful, as always.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Thank you, Cressida.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.92,0:23:36.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You could have chosen anyone.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:36.46,0:23:38.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You have gentlemen lined up{\i0}\N{\i1}to pay you tribute.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.30,0:23:42.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yet you did not hesitate to steal{\i0}\N{\i1}my chance for happiness away, did you?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.93,0:23:46.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I knew the marriage market{\i0}\N{\i1}would make rivals of us,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:47.06,0:23:48.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but I never thought you capable{\i0}\N{\i1}of being my enemy.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:49.06,0:23:51.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The man made his choice, Cressida.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:53.15,0:23:54.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What did you expect me to do?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:03.74,0:24:07.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Miss Bridgerton.{\i0}\N{\i1}You look absolutely exquisite, as always.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:07.49,0:24:09.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Thank you, Your Highness.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:09.37,0:24:11.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I hope there's room on your dance card{\i0}\N{\i1}for the two of us.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:11.91,0:24:13.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I believe there is.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:28.93,0:24:31.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}["Second Waltz"{\i0}\N{\i1}by Dmitri Shostakovich ends]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:38.15,0:24:38.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Jeffries!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:40.19,0:24:41.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:41.40,0:24:43.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why is this painting here{\i0}\N{\i1}and not at Somerset House?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:44.03,0:24:45.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Have you forgotten, sir?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:45.36,0:24:47.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You requested it returned to you,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:47.82,0:24:50.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}an endeavor that was no small feat{\i0}\N{\i1}to arrange, I might add.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:53.41,0:24:54.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[dramatic music plays]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:18.10,0:25:19.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mr. Bridgerton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:20.36,0:25:21.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Come in, come in.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:21.94,0:25:22.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Thank you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:31.87,0:25:35.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I do not know what I {\i0}<span style="style2">was {\i0}{\i1}expecting,{\i0}\N{\i1}but it surely was not this.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:35.62,0:25:38.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, simply a gathering{\i0}\N{\i1}of like-minded souls.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:38.92,0:25:41.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Here, let me show you{\i0}\N{\i1}what I've been working on.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:42.17,0:25:45.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}They speak of war abroad as if{\i0}\N{\i1}it will distract from inequities at home.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:45.34,0:25:47.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}They do not need a war to be distracted.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:47.59,0:25:49.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why, this Whistledown's enough{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:49.18,0:25:51.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to turn their eyes{\i0}\N{\i1}from the needs of ordinary people.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:52.06,0:25:53.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Henry] What do you think?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:53.93,0:25:54.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Benedict sighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:56.56,0:25:57.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Hmm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:57.69,0:25:59.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's a far cry{\i0}\N{\i1}from Somerset House, I must say.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:59.98,0:26:01.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I shall take that as a compliment.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:01.40,0:26:02.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both chuckle]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:02.32,0:26:04.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And I must say, I'm truly jealous.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:05.24,0:26:06.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is this your life?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:07.99,0:26:10.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There are advantages{\i0}\N{\i1}to being the second-born.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:11.24,0:26:12.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Heirs have the responsibility.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:13.29,0:26:15.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Second sons have the fun.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[both chuckle]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:15.54,0:26:16.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}So…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:17.33,0:26:18.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}why not go have some fun?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:42.90,0:26:44.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[exhales slowly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:55.58,0:26:58.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[singing "Belle nuit, ô nuit d'amour"{\i0}\N{\i1}in French]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:04.21,0:27:07.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[guests chattering quietly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:38.95,0:27:40.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Violet] Anthony?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:40.29,0:27:41.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Anthony.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:41.75,0:27:44.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This is Miss Addington,{\i0}\N{\i1}the Earl of Lindsay's niece.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:44.63,0:27:45.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Pleasure.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Mm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:45.96,0:27:48.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Violet chuckles] There, you see?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:56.76,0:27:57.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[chuckles awkwardly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:01.43,0:28:03.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Quite the affair, Lady Trowbridge.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:03.73,0:28:05.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You have such, uh…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:05.69,0:28:08.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[chuckles] …striking taste.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:08.15,0:28:10.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What a compliment, Lady Featherington,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:10.15,0:28:11.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}especially from you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:12.70,0:28:13.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Featherington] Mm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:13.91,0:28:17.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Philippa, should you not be{\i0}\N{\i1}on the dance floor with Mr. Finch?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:17.70,0:28:18.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Philippa sobs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:19.29,0:28:20.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Dry your eyes.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:20.25,0:28:22.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Such constant commotion{\i0}\N{\i1}with this one, Mama.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:23.04,0:28:25.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Mr. Finch won't so much as meet my eye.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Prudence scoffs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:25.96,0:28:27.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Papa told him something, and now…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:29.05,0:28:30.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I loved him. [sobs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:36.59,0:28:38.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Whatever did you say to Mr. Finch?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:38.51,0:28:40.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He may not be a lord,{\i0}\N{\i1}but he's perfectly suitable,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:41.06,0:28:42.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and Phillipa has no other suitors.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:42.64,0:28:44.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Then we shall wait until next season.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:46.10,0:28:47.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}With two others unwed?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:47.56,0:28:50.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}They can all wait until next season,{\i0}\N{\i1}as far as I'm concerned.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:50.40,0:28:53.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Could you truly wish{\i0}\N{\i1}to embarrass me further tonight?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:53.65,0:28:55.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I would advise against it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:15.18,0:29:17.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What are you doing in my room?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:18.14,0:29:19.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh… Uh…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:19.55,0:29:22.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mama asked me to retrieve{\i0}\N{\i1}the latest copy of Lady Whistledown.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:22.85,0:29:27.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She wanted to count how many times Daphne{\i0}\N{\i1}and Prince Friedrich had been mentioned.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:27.77,0:29:29.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The viscountess is at the Trowbridge ball.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:29.65,0:29:32.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She did not seem particularly pleased{\i0}\N{\i1}about Prince Friedrich.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:33.03,0:29:34.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[chuckles nervously]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:34.44,0:29:36.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why do you have them,{\i0}\N{\i1}all of these Whistledowns?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:36.61,0:29:38.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Must I explain myself to you?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:39.45,0:29:40.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yes…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:41.28,0:29:42.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}you must.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:42.20,0:29:44.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}After all, I am a Bridgerton,{\i0}\N{\i1}so therefore your mistress.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:45.75,0:29:48.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I wiped your bottom{\i0}\N{\i1}when you were in leading strings,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:48.88,0:29:51.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and I… I do not appreciate your tone.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:51.17,0:29:55.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I asked you once, and I ask again,{\i0}\N{\i1}what are you doing in my room, Eloise?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:55.72,0:29:57.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Thinking perhaps {\i0}<span style="style2">you {\i0}{\i1}are Lady Whistledown.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:59.01,0:30:00.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[laughing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:01.64,0:30:04.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Or… if not you,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:04.43,0:30:06.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}then perhaps another servant type.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:07.02,0:30:08.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Are you not meant to be the smart one?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:09.02,0:30:10.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I beg your pardon?{\i0}\N{\i1}-[laughs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:10.73,0:30:15.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You believe a servant would ever have{\i0}\N{\i1}the time to be Lady Whistledown,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:15.36,0:30:17.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}with all the work we must do?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:17.20,0:30:19.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[laughing continues]{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Eloise chuckles awkwardly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:20.91,0:30:26.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You believe I would be working for you{\i0}\N{\i1}if I had all the money Whistledown does?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:26.20,0:30:28.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[Eloise sighs ironically]{\i0}\N{\i1}-Oh! Oh!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:28.67,0:30:31.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, it hurts. [laughing continues]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:33.46,0:30:34.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Get out.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:39.59,0:30:41.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[guests chattering]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:52.69,0:30:54.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Our host looks a bit fussy.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:55.23,0:30:57.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do you think if he goes to bed,{\i0}\N{\i1}we all have to leave?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:57.49,0:30:58.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Penelope chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:58.40,0:31:01.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's lucky the lady produced an heir{\i0}\N{\i1}before the old earl croaked, no?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:01.87,0:31:03.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Lucky, indeed.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:03.91,0:31:06.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But do you not think{\i0}\N{\i1}the boy bears a passing resemblance{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:06.24,0:31:07.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to Lady Trowbridge's footman?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:07.87,0:31:08.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Penelope!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:09.96,0:31:11.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What a barb!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:18.17,0:31:20.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've tried to get in front{\i0}\N{\i1}of Miss Thompson all night.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:20.43,0:31:22.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Surely she cannot be interested{\i0}\N{\i1}in Lord Rutledge, can she?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:23.01,0:31:25.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I think the only thing{\i0}\N{\i1}Miss Thompson is interested in{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:25.22,0:31:26.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}is a swift rescue, indeed.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:27.43,0:31:29.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I believe you are right.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:29.23,0:31:31.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, Colin, I did not mean--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:38.48,0:31:39.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Another?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:39.40,0:31:41.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[chuckles] I do believe a third dance{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:41.45,0:31:43.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}would be considered improper, my lord.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:43.57,0:31:47.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You need not continue{\i0}\N{\i1}to prove your virtue to me, my girl.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:47.29,0:31:50.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There are other things{\i0}\N{\i1}a man looks for in a wife.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:50.50,0:31:52.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Miss Thompson. A dance?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:56.88,0:31:58.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Are you well recovered, Miss Thompson?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:59.59,0:32:01.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, yes. Um, I was quite ill.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:01.76,0:32:04.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And what a suspicious illness{\i0}\N{\i1}you came down with.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:05.18,0:32:06.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It seems to have manifested{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:06.80,0:32:09.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}as a walking spittle factory{\i0}\N{\i1}with very large teeth.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:12.35,0:32:14.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Am I the only one who can see it?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Alas, I can as well.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:14.98,0:32:17.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But spin me away,{\i0}\N{\i1}and perhaps I shall recover.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:18.86,0:32:20.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both laughing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:24.95,0:32:26.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}They appear to be enjoying themselves.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:26.66,0:32:30.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yes. My brother Colin certainly knows{\i0}\N{\i1}how to make things memorable.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:32.25,0:32:34.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, perhaps I may do the same.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:36.54,0:32:39.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know we've only known each other{\i0}\N{\i1}a short time, Miss Bridgerton,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:39.63,0:32:41.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but from the moment{\i0}\N{\i1}I laid eyes on you, I, uh--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:48.18,0:32:50.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Ah! There you are.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Here I am, Your Highness.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:52.35,0:32:53.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}As I was saying,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:54.14,0:32:56.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}some in Prussia believe I have run away,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:56.69,0:32:59.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but the truth is I left{\i0}\N{\i1}to find someone to start a life with.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:00.02,0:33:02.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-To have a family with.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[gasps]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:07.32,0:33:08.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[gasps]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:10.20,0:33:14.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And so I find myself left{\i0}\N{\i1}with one question to ask.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:18.50,0:33:19.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Miss Bridgerton--{\i0}\N{\i1}-I need a moment.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:22.09,0:33:24.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}To refresh myself, Your Highness.{\i0}\N{\i1}[breathes nervously]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:24.63,0:33:26.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Miss Bridgerton, are you yet engaged?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:27.93,0:33:31.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You must set me up with one{\i0}\N{\i1}of those brothers I hear the prince has.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:31.97,0:33:34.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do watch where you are flying, angel.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:34.93,0:33:35.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[exhales nervously]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:37.94,0:33:39.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[gasping]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:45.70,0:33:47.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[grunts loudly, panting]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:50.07,0:33:51.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon] Miss Bridgerton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:53.16,0:33:54.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[gasps]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:56.25,0:33:57.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What are you doing here?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:00.96,0:34:04.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I thought you were leaving London.{\i0}\N{\i1}-I was. I am.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:05.88,0:34:07.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I came to say goodbye.{\i0}\N{\i1}-To whom?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:08.05,0:34:10.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-To you.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Your goodbye is wholly unnecessary.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:12.06,0:34:13.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We are not friends.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:13.81,0:34:15.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We never were friends,{\i0}\N{\i1}as you made abundantly clear.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:15.93,0:34:18.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-And I am sorry for that.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Please, do not apologize.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:20.27,0:34:23.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I shall not be led once more{\i0}\N{\i1}by you from this direction to that.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:24.40,0:34:28.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You are my friend. You are not my friend.{\i0}\N{\i1}You are a rake. You are not a rake.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:28.24,0:34:30.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-You are sorry--{\i0}\N{\i1}-I am sorry.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:30.11,0:34:31.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That is very well.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:32.83,0:34:36.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But you should know that your apology{\i0}\N{\i1}has absolutely no effect on my life,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:36.25,0:34:38.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}nor does your leaving London.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:39.04,0:34:40.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am marrying the prince.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:40.96,0:34:43.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I shall be very happy, indeed.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:46.71,0:34:48.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Will you be? Happy?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:48.88,0:34:50.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why would I not be?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:51.80,0:34:53.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Prince Friedrich is kind…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:54.47,0:34:55.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and adoring…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:56.43,0:34:58.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and he knows what he wants.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:59.48,0:35:02.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He is a good man,{\i0}\N{\i1}and he will make a wonderful father.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:02.31,0:35:04.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And so you truly believe him{\i0}\N{\i1}the best man for you?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:04.90,0:35:06.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}How dare you question my choices?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:08.28,0:35:10.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}They are my choices to make, not yours.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:10.99,0:35:14.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I do not question your choice{\i0}\N{\i1}to rake across the continent,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:14.58,0:35:15.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}forlorn and alone.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:16.95,0:35:20.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I do not have to explain myself to you.{\i0}\N{\i1}I do not owe you anything.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:21.17,0:35:24.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He is perfect for me.{\i0}\N{\i1}I am going to be princess!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:31.30,0:35:32.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Are you going to say anything?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:38.60,0:35:39.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, then, leave.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:41.94,0:35:42.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[groans]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:43.65,0:35:44.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Very well.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:47.32,0:35:48.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon] Miss Bridgerton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:49.19,0:35:50.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Miss Bridgerton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:51.57,0:35:52.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Miss Bridgerton!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:59.16,0:36:00.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Come back to the party.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:01.08,0:36:02.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Stop walking!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:02.29,0:36:04.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Stop following me.{\i0}\N{\i1}-It is not safe out here.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:05.71,0:36:09.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I forbid you to go any further.{\i0}\N{\i1}-You cannot tell me what to do.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:09.26,0:36:10.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon] Daphne…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:11.47,0:36:13.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Will you not listen?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:21.93,0:36:23.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne breaths tremulously]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:25.27,0:36:26.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My most sincere apologies.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:26.90,0:36:28.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne panting]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:28.44,0:36:29.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon] I…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:31.40,0:36:32.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:42.04,0:36:44.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne gasping] Oh!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:49.34,0:36:50.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both grunting, moaning]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:53.84,0:36:54.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne gasps]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:58.35,0:36:59.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Bastard!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:59.68,0:37:01.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[Anthony grunts]{\i0}\N{\i1}-Anthony!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:03.18,0:37:04.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne gasps]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:07.90,0:37:08.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You will marry her.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:10.11,0:37:11.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-What?{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Anthony] Immediately.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:11.86,0:37:13.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We can only hope{\i0}\N{\i1}no one saw you take such liberties,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:13.78,0:37:15.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and my sister{\i0}\N{\i1}is saved further mortification.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:15.61,0:37:17.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-You will marry her!{\i0}\N{\i1}-Brother!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:17.49,0:37:19.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[panting] I cannot marry her.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:22.37,0:37:25.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You have defiled her innocence,{\i0}\N{\i1}and now you refuse her hand?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:27.38,0:37:29.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I knew you were a rake, Hastings,{\i0}\N{\i1}never thought a villain.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:29.67,0:37:31.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I cannot marry her.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:35.59,0:37:37.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Then you leave me no choice.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:38.05,0:37:39.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I must demand satisfaction.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:40.64,0:37:43.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A duel? Anthony, you cannot--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:43.22,0:37:44.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He dishonors you, sister.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:44.77,0:37:48.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He dishonors you and me{\i0}\N{\i1}and the very Bridgerton name.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:49.15,0:37:51.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have misjudged you, indeed.{\i0}\N{\i1}You have duped us both,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:51.73,0:37:54.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but I shall not see{\i0}\N{\i1}my sister pay for my own misdeeds.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:54.19,0:37:56.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-We will settle this as gentlemen.{\i0}\N{\i1}-I understand.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:57.66,0:37:59.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I shall see you at dawn.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:01.16,0:38:02.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I do not understand.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:04.12,0:38:07.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You would rather die than marry me?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:09.29,0:38:10.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am truly sorry.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:12.88,0:38:14.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Anthony] We need to go, Daph,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:14.71,0:38:16.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}before anyone should see us.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:24.52,0:38:26.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[distorted sigh]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:30.48,0:38:32.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[distorted heartbeat]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:32.32,0:38:34.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[distorted laughing, chattering]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:39.78,0:38:40.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[distortion ends]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:40.95,0:38:44.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Violet] Champagne!{\i0}\N{\i1}It sounds like "sham" and "pain."{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:44.16,0:38:46.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is quite amusing, really. [laughs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:46.66,0:38:49.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Our sister has a headache.{\i0}\N{\i1}I am taking her home.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:49.58,0:38:52.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-See to Mother, will you?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Daphne, you look unwell.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:52.84,0:38:54.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Did you catch a chill in the garden?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:05.06,0:39:06.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[bristles brushing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:16.48,0:39:17.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Hmm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:17.99,0:39:19.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-You have great potential.{\i0}\N{\i1}-It's nothing.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:20.28,0:39:22.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Though,{\i0}\N{\i1}for such a staunch critic of others,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:22.16,0:39:24.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}you certainly lack{\i0}\N{\i1}a clear eye for your own work.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:24.16,0:39:26.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's the lines.{\i0}\N{\i1}Not what they're supposed to be.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:26.24,0:39:28.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Take the compliment, Bridgerton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:28.87,0:39:31.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There is no expectation or judgment here.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:32.17,0:39:34.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You left all of that back in Mayfair.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:34.79,0:39:35.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Benedict chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:36.30,0:39:38.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You can feel free to be yourself here…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:39.30,0:39:40.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}if that's what you should like.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:41.47,0:39:43.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's what works for me, at least.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:43.72,0:39:47.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And I haven't been dissatisfied{\i0}\N{\i1}with my lines in… well, quite some time.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:47.52,0:39:48.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Benedict chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:48.60,0:39:51.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Well, I've done worse, I suppose, really.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Mm. Fair enough.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:52.69,0:39:55.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I seem to have enjoyed myself{\i0}\N{\i1}too much this evening.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:56.36,0:39:57.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I should be on my way.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:57.90,0:39:59.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[exhales deeply] As you wish.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:59.90,0:40:04.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But know you are welcome back any time{\i0}\N{\i1}for practice or even conversation.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:04.91,0:40:06.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both laughing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:07.70,0:40:08.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'll see you out.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:17.13,0:40:20.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I knew something was amiss{\i0}\N{\i1}when he insisted we keep Miss Thompson,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:20.42,0:40:22.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but did I quarrel with him? No.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:22.09,0:40:23.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I did what I was told, I did my best.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:23.68,0:40:26.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But getting rid{\i0}\N{\i1}of my dear Philippa's one and only suitor…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:26.18,0:40:29.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Under no circumstances. Intolerable man!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:30.31,0:40:31.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Guard the door.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:31.56,0:40:33.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What exactly{\i0}\N{\i1}are you hoping to find, ma'am?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:33.60,0:40:36.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I shan't know that,{\i0}\N{\i1}Mrs. Varley, until I find it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:39.61,0:40:41.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Pen, he is kind and funny{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:41.78,0:40:43.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and a surprisingly accomplished dancer.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:44.07,0:40:47.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And, well, I'm sure you've seen him{\i0}\N{\i1}with the small Bridgertons.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:47.58,0:40:49.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He will be a wonderful father.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:50.04,0:40:51.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[chuckles lightly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:51.83,0:40:54.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Surely, though,{\i0}\N{\i1}Colin is a tad young for marriage.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:54.79,0:40:56.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You do need someone{\i0}\N{\i1}who will propose soon.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:57.00,0:40:59.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But that is why{\i0}\N{\i1}Mr. Bridgerton is so perfect.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:59.71,0:41:02.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Did you see the way he rescued me tonight?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:02.30,0:41:06.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He's not like the other young men{\i0}\N{\i1}who play games and guard their affections.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:07.47,0:41:08.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He is eager.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:09.85,0:41:12.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Pen, I believe he will propose soon.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:13.02,0:41:15.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I shan't have to marry Rutledge.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[forced chuckle]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:17.27,0:41:20.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, I am sorry.{\i0}\N{\i1}Am I keeping you awake with all this talk?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:20.23,0:41:22.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yes, I do feel sleep coming over me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:23.28,0:41:24.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But, Pen…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:25.40,0:41:26.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the best part is,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:27.53,0:41:29.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}when we wed,{\i0}\N{\i1}I'll be able to stay in town.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:29.78,0:41:33.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And since you and Eloise are so close,{\i0}\N{\i1}we will all practically be sisters.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:34.08,0:41:35.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Imagine that.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:35.21,0:41:36.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[exhales joyously]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:38.29,0:41:39.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[door opens]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:40.25,0:41:41.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[door closes]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:43.55,0:41:45.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sobbing breaths]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:54.31,0:41:55.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[light tapping]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:56.89,0:41:57.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[light tapping]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:04.40,0:42:05.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have a theory.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:05.90,0:42:06.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[strained chuckle]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:06.90,0:42:09.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Eloise, it is quite late.{\i0}\N{\i1}-A good theory about Lady Whistledown.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:09.74,0:42:13.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I thought she had to be a servant,{\i0}\N{\i1}but I was wrong, quite wrong.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:13.33,0:42:16.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Because who truly has{\i0}\N{\i1}the time and means to be that remarkable?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:16.12,0:42:17.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Who would be invited{\i0}\N{\i1}to all of the parties,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:18.00,0:42:20.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}able to hear things unnoticed by others?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:20.21,0:42:21.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps we can discuss it tomorrow.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:21.67,0:42:24.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Lady Whistledown is someone free{\i0}\N{\i1}and unencumbered by society.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:24.38,0:42:26.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She is a single woman of means.{\i0}\N{\i1}Better yet, she is a widow,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:26.97,0:42:29.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}who would be invited to all of the events{\i0}\N{\i1}but not paid any attention.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:30.01,0:42:31.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}While you were at the ball--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:31.26,0:42:32.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Eloise, I do not care!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:34.85,0:42:37.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}People have real problems,{\i0}\N{\i1}mature problems,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:37.56,0:42:38.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}problems that have nothing to do{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:38.98,0:42:40.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}with the secret identity{\i0}\N{\i1}of some silly writer.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:42.19,0:42:43.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And you are so mature now?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:44.57,0:42:45.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, I am of age.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:45.82,0:42:47.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am out in society.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:47.32,0:42:50.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Therefore, I have more important,{\i0}\N{\i1}mature things to worry about.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:50.20,0:42:51.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Like what?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Like marriage.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:51.74,0:42:53.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-You do not care about marriage.{\i0}\N{\i1}-What if I do?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:55.41,0:42:57.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I cannot expect you to understand.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:57.54,0:42:59.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Not everyone can be a pretty Bridgerton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:04.04,0:43:05.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Eloise, I did not--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:05.80,0:43:06.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Eloise, wait!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:14.39,0:43:16.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Thank you, Humboldt.{\i0}\N{\i1}No need to send anyone up.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:17.43,0:43:19.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I want you to know{\i0}\N{\i1}I am not angry with you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:20.02,0:43:22.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I do not blame you for what transpired.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:22.35,0:43:24.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do not treat me like a child.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:24.57,0:43:25.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I did this.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:25.82,0:43:29.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-He took advantage of you.{\i0}\N{\i1}-No less than I took liberties with him.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:29.11,0:43:30.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You do not understand.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:31.03,0:43:34.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I should have protected you better.{\i0}\N{\i1}I knew his true nature from the start.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:34.70,0:43:36.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You think that just because I am a woman,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:36.87,0:43:39.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am incapable of making my own choices?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:40.12,0:43:41.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is that it, brother?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:42.33,0:43:45.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do you even care{\i0}\N{\i1}that Simon has dishonored me, as you say,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:45.38,0:43:48.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}or is it your own male pride{\i0}\N{\i1}that you seek to satisfy?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:48.96,0:43:51.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-You are to go on up to bed.{\i0}\N{\i1}-You cannot duel him.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:51.84,0:43:54.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is illegal, to name but one reason.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:54.26,0:43:56.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You could both be arrested,{\i0}\N{\i1}let alone killed.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:58.97,0:44:01.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-There must be another way.{\i0}\N{\i1}-What would you have me do?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:02.23,0:44:03.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I do not take this decision lightly,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:03.73,0:44:06.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but this is the way{\i0}\N{\i1}things are handled amongst gentlemen.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:06.27,0:44:08.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-If this were to become known--{\i0}\N{\i1}-I could live with that.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:09.23,0:44:12.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What I could not live with{\i0}\N{\i1}is the duke's death on my hands.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:13.57,0:44:16.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Nor yours, however tempting{\i0}\N{\i1}that may be at this very moment.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:16.45,0:44:19.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is more than just your honor at stake.{\i0}\N{\i1}It is your sisters', too,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:19.20,0:44:20.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the entire family name.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:20.70,0:44:21.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It has been decided.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:21.83,0:44:22.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, this is madness!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:24.75,0:44:25.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What is it?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:26.46,0:44:27.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You and I need to talk.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:28.30,0:44:29.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Daphne, bed.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:32.30,0:44:33.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[door slams]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:34.80,0:44:37.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[panting deeply, growls]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:37.97,0:44:39.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I will need you to stand as my second.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:41.43,0:44:43.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What if you get yourself killed?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:43.27,0:44:45.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Then the title and estates{\i0}\N{\i1}will pass to you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:48.11,0:44:50.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-And if you kill Hastings?{\i0}\N{\i1}-I shall have to leave the country.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:51.03,0:44:53.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You'll be head of the family{\i0}\N{\i1}in every way that matters.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:54.91,0:44:55.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[muffled chuckling]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:56.99,0:44:59.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Colin] Of course not.{\i0}\N{\i1}You are clearly sober.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:59.58,0:45:01.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Violet laughs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:03.08,0:45:06.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And I'm sober enough to know{\i0}\N{\i1}when you're being impertinent.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:07.21,0:45:09.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Good night, dear.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Good night, Mother.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:13.30,0:45:14.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Come here.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:14.43,0:45:16.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Good God. Did someone die?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:17.05,0:45:19.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[clattering]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:20.64,0:45:21.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What are you doing?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:21.89,0:45:24.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I find myself{\i0}\N{\i1}in rather desperate need of a drink.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:24.56,0:45:26.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And this was the only place{\i0}\N{\i1}you could find one?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:31.98,0:45:33.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Are you not supposed{\i0}\N{\i1}to be on a ship by now?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:33.94,0:45:34.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Change of plans.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:37.57,0:45:40.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}For brandy this good, you need{\i0}\N{\i1}to actually tell me what is going on.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:42.87,0:45:45.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am to meet Anthony Bridgerton at dawn.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:53.63,0:45:57.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Whatever the insult, apologize,{\i0}\N{\i1}and he will surely be a forgiving man.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:57.76,0:46:00.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Not when it comes to his sister.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:02.39,0:46:05.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Exactly how insulted was she?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:06.89,0:46:08.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[exhales tremulously]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:15.36,0:46:17.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I shall need another{\i0}\N{\i1}if I am to be your second.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:17.24,0:46:19.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I cannot let you.{\i0}\N{\i1}-You cannot stop me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:19.82,0:46:21.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[tense music plays]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:49.39,0:46:51.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I believe you may have strayed too far{\i0}\N{\i1}from home tonight.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:52.02,0:46:53.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Siena, please.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:54.40,0:46:56.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We cannot be together. I know that now.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:56.19,0:46:57.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This world shall not permit it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:57.69,0:47:00.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But what if we were to find ourselves{\i0}\N{\i1}in another situation,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:00.32,0:47:02.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}at a place{\i0}\N{\i1}where you and I might be accepted,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:02.49,0:47:05.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}with none of the shame nor recriminations{\i0}\N{\i1}that this society grants us.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:05.33,0:47:06.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Would you have me then?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:06.45,0:47:08.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You talk in dreams, my lord,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:08.71,0:47:10.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and yet you deprive me{\i0}\N{\i1}the luxury of sleep.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:10.75,0:47:12.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I duel at dawn.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:16.96,0:47:18.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}An affair of honor?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:18.22,0:47:20.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If I live to see sunrise, I am free…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:21.68,0:47:25.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}free of society, free of these rules,{\i0}\N{\i1}the very ones that keep us apart.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:25.18,0:47:27.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We could go together,{\i0}\N{\i1}away from all this, Siena.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:35.52,0:47:36.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My apologies.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:38.36,0:47:40.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've taxed your patience{\i0}\N{\i1}for the last time.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:44.32,0:47:45.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Anthony moans]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:47.49,0:47:49.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both breathing heavily]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:58.17,0:47:59.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both grunting, moaning]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:04.47,0:48:05.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:17.36,0:48:19.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Wh-- What are you doing in here?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Hush.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:20.03,0:48:24.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I found your ledgers,{\i0}\N{\i1}hidden under old newspapers, no less.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:26.53,0:48:27.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[exhales tremulously]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:28.74,0:48:30.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know of every transaction…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:32.21,0:48:33.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}every financial account.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:34.00,0:48:35.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Y-- You do not know--{\i0}\N{\i1}-I know…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:36.75,0:48:37.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}everything.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:38.84,0:48:40.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know about your gambling.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:40.80,0:48:42.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know about your debts.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:42.47,0:48:45.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know that you have spent all our money.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:45.18,0:48:47.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I shall not--{\i0}\N{\i1}-Including our girls' dowries!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:53.02,0:48:57.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is that not why you rejected{\i0}\N{\i1}that perfectly acceptable Mr. Finch{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:57.61,0:48:59.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}for our dear Philippa?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:59.32,0:49:02.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is it not why we continue{\i0}\N{\i1}to keep Miss Thompson in our home?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:02.95,0:49:04.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You owe her father too.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:04.45,0:49:07.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}So the question{\i0}\N{\i1}certainly is not what I know!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:08.28,0:49:09.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:11.08,0:49:12.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The question is…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:13.96,0:49:16.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}what are {\i0}<span style="style2">you {\i0}{\i1}going to do about it?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:18.92,0:49:20.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[sobs]{\i0}\N{\i1}-My lord?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:21.76,0:49:22.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-My lord?{\i0}\N{\i1}-[weeping]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:28.60,0:49:29.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sniffs loudly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:29.89,0:49:30.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Archibald…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:31.01,0:49:32.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've have failed you!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:33.60,0:49:35.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've-- I've--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:35.19,0:49:37.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have failed our daughters!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:39.06,0:49:39.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:41.78,0:49:43.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I do not know what to do.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:44.53,0:49:46.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sobbing] Portia…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:47.99,0:49:49.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I don't know what to do.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:55.25,0:49:57.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[weeping, sniffing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:15.39,0:50:17.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[tense music plays]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:18.10,0:50:18.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[kisses]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:56.73,0:50:58.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[tense music continues]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:07.99,0:51:09.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Where have they gone?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Daph…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:09.49,0:51:11.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Tell me where this duel takes place.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Why would I do that?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:11.82,0:51:15.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-So that I may prevent it from happening.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Hastings has done you a grave dishonor.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:15.37,0:51:17.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Surely you wish to see him pay.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Not with his life.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:17.58,0:51:20.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It will not come to that.{\i0}\N{\i1}The duke will remember his honor{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:20.08,0:51:22.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}once he finds himself{\i0}\N{\i1}on the deadly end of a pistol.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:22.33,0:51:23.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And if he does not?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:23.63,0:51:26.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}They will both do the gentlemanly thing{\i0}\N{\i1}and fire their pistols wide.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:26.71,0:51:30.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Allow them to bring this ugly business{\i0}\N{\i1}to a conclusion themselves.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:30.43,0:51:33.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[groans] Do you know how many times{\i0}\N{\i1}I have heard that said?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:33.89,0:51:35.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}To leave the men to their business{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:35.68,0:51:38.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and to not concern myself{\i0}\N{\i1}with such weighty affairs,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:39.35,0:51:42.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}whose affairs are my future, my family.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:43.52,0:51:47.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Anthony is too angry to fire wide,{\i0}\N{\i1}and Simon is too stubborn to yield.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:47.61,0:51:49.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You did not see them in that garden.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:49.11,0:51:51.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}No, I did not,{\i0}\N{\i1}and neither did anyone else.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:51.28,0:51:53.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You should be happy{\i0}\N{\i1}that no one saw anything.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:53.45,0:51:57.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Daphne, you look unwell.{\i0}\N{\i1}Did you catch a chill in the garden?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:58.37,0:51:59.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Only, someone did see.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:01.62,0:52:02.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Cressida Cowper.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:04.46,0:52:06.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Colin, you must tell me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:07.50,0:52:08.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Where have they gone?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:21.69,0:52:23.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Doctor, I appreciate{\i0}\N{\i1}your attendance and discretion.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:24.06,0:52:25.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You have my blunt?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:28.07,0:52:31.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Very well.{\i0}\N{\i1}Try not to go dying while I am present.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:31.11,0:52:34.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If the goal is merely to wound,{\i0}\N{\i1}where should my brother aim?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:34.16,0:52:37.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You think you have the skill{\i0}\N{\i1}to guide the path of a moving bullet?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:37.37,0:52:40.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Then you are either a fool{\i0}\N{\i1}or the king's finest marksman.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:41.04,0:52:41.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Which is it?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:45.29,0:52:46.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[horses neighing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:54.43,0:52:56.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have one last matter{\i0}\N{\i1}to discuss with you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:56.43,0:52:58.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You have already provided{\i0}\N{\i1}ample instruction.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:58.43,0:53:00.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Contact the solicitor{\i0}\N{\i1}and safeguard our sisters' dowries.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:00.68,0:53:01.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}An additional task.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:01.60,0:53:04.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}In the top drawer of my desk,{\i0}\N{\i1}you shall find the name of a lady.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:05.23,0:53:08.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If I die, you must ensure{\i0}\N{\i1}she is provided for. Do you swear?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:09.11,0:53:10.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Benedict, do--{\i0}\N{\i1}-I swear.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:20.29,0:53:21.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Brother--{\i0}\N{\i1}-That is all.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:29.84,0:53:32.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Is there anything you need from me?{\i0}\N{\i1}-My affairs are in order.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:37.80,0:53:39.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[tense music intensifies]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:08.00,0:54:10.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}For what it is worth, I am sorry.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:10.67,0:54:12.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your apology is worth nothing to me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:21.51,0:54:23.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[pistols cocking]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:34.28,0:54:35.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Ready!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:35.36,0:54:36.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Ready!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:06.89,0:55:08.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[tense music crescendos]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:09.02,0:55:10.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Stop!{\i0}\N{\i1}-[gunshot]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:10.31,0:55:12.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[horse whinnies]{\i0}\N{\i1}-Daphne! [gasps]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:12.69,0:55:14.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Sister!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:14.11,0:55:15.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Sister! Stand aside!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:20.20,0:55:22.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Oh, good God.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Daphne panting]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:22.16,0:55:24.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Are you hurt? Tell me!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:24.24,0:55:28.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am perfectly well,{\i0}\N{\i1}no thanks to you idiots.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:28.20,0:55:30.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-What are you playing at?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Says the man who just shot at me!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:30.46,0:55:31.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You rode into the middle of a duel!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:33.42,0:55:34.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I require a moment with the duke.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:34.92,0:55:37.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Daphne--{\i0}\N{\i1}-I require a moment with the duke.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:37.67,0:55:38.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Make it brief.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:40.88,0:55:42.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You should not have come.{\i0}\N{\i1}My mind's not changed.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:42.80,0:55:43.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It must.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:44.30,0:55:46.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If not for your sake, then mine.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:46.85,0:55:48.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Simon, we were seen.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:48.81,0:55:50.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Cressida Cowper{\i0}\N{\i1}witnessed us in the garden.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:51.02,0:55:52.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She knows.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:52.27,0:55:55.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is not merely your own life{\i0}\N{\i1}that hangs in the balance now.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:55.48,0:55:58.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you do not marry me,{\i0}\N{\i1}I shall be ruined.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:00.61,0:56:01.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Daphne, I cannot.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:03.03,0:56:04.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Did you not hear me?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:05.03,0:56:06.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Someone knows what we have done,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:07.08,0:56:08.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}someone who will surely talk.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:11.37,0:56:16.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What possible reason could you have{\i0}\N{\i1}to condemn me to shame and reproach?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:18.00,0:56:18.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do you truly…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:20.26,0:56:22.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do you truly hold me in such low regard?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:22.55,0:56:25.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is because I regard you so highly{\i0}\N{\i1}that I cannot marry you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:28.72,0:56:30.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know you do not love me,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:31.31,0:56:33.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but I never thought{\i0}\N{\i1}you could despise me so.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:33.40,0:56:34.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Daphne…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:39.11,0:56:40.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You must know, if we were to wed…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:43.57,0:56:45.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I can never give you children.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:47.45,0:56:50.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is your dream to be a mother,{\i0}\N{\i1}is it not?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:50.91,0:56:53.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}To have a household{\i0}\N{\i1}full of love and laughter,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:53.08,0:56:55.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}like the one you have known all your life?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:57.13,0:56:58.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You deserve nothing less.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:59.92,0:57:03.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You deserve everything your heart desires.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:04.22,0:57:05.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But I cannot provide it for you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:07.55,0:57:09.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Nor could I ever ask such a sacrifice.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:10.56,0:57:13.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Please, Daphne, for your own sake…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:14.81,0:57:16.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}you must stand aside…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:17.52,0:57:19.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and let your brother finish this.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:21.23,0:57:23.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We must resume{\i0}\N{\i1}before someone should find us.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:29.28,0:57:30.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There will be no need to resume.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:36.50,0:57:38.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The duke and I are to be married.{\i0}
